"],"finding":"The plan frames the invariant as gating-lane extras vs sweep-lane extras, but the two lane groups are ALREADY heterogeneous on the current green tree — the gating `test` lane installs `dev+reviewbot+ui+grounding-terraform` (_build-and-test.yml:495) while sweep lanes install `dev,reviewbot,ui` (test.yml:234/267/312) and the lower-bound lane installs `dev,agents` (test.yml:338, no reviewbot/ui/grounding-terraform, but adds `agents`). A mechanism that simply diffs the extra sets would therefore have to treat every one of these existing divergences (agents, reviewbot, ui, grounding-terraform) as a DELIBERATE declaration on day one, or it fails on a green tree. The plan does not surface this baseline so the implementer can size the deliberate-divergence declaration (AC2) correctly.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6fe91df28cc4a698","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Why this is worth its own ticket' / AC1 + AC2","norm_id":"nedfe880eca38e767","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes a set-diff check; it fails immediately on main because agents/reviewbot/ui/grounding-terraform already differ across the lanes, forcing a large intended-divergence registry that was not anticipated."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a default home/shape for the 'intended-divergence' declaration (e.g. a sentinel comment on the sweep install line or a small allow-list file the parity test reads), so AC2's 'expressible and passes' path is concrete.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'WITHOUT an explicit, in-tree declaration that the divergence is intended'","AC2: 'A DELIBERATE divergence remains expressible and passes'","Plan explicitly declines to prescribe the mechanism: 'the acceptance criteria below do not prescribe the mechanism' — legitimate design latitude, but the declaration's home is still needed to test AC2"],"finding":"AC1/AC2 require an 'explicit, in-tree declaration that the divergence is intended', but the plan states no default location or shape for that declaration, so the executor must invent where the allow-list/annotation lives before AC2 can be exercised.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f736556cded841ede","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1 and AC2","norm_id":"nac56e8693ec62c0a","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor writes the check but has no stated convention for where the 'intended divergence' marker should live, risking a marker the parity test cannot find"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Note in the plan that the existing `_INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES` allowlist + derive-and-diff pattern in test_no_drift_script_gate_is_verified_only_in_branch_ci is the established shape for AC1–AC3, and direct the implementer to extend/mirror it rather than build a new intended-divergence mechanism.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'an explicit, in-tree declaration that the divergence is intended' — structurally identical to the existing `_INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES: set[str]` allowlist (test_ci_workflow_parity.py:142-154), whose docstring already reads 'Add an entry only with a written reason.'","test_no_drift_script_gate_is_verified_only_in_branch_ci (test_ci_workflow_parity.py:1066-1083) already implements: regex-extract a set from each lane, subtract a documented-exception set, assert `not missing`, and name what diverged — exactly AC1+AC3.","The plan itself defers mechanism ('the acceptance criteria below do not prescribe the mechanism'), so this is a reuse pointer, not a duplicate-abstraction assertion."],"finding":"AC1/AC2 describe a derive-both-sets / diff / allow-a-documented-exception parity mechanism that already exists in the same file the plan names (test_no_drift_script_gate_is_verified_only_in_branch_ci + _INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES); the plan doesn't point implementers at it, risking a from-scratch reinvention of an established, understood pattern.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd32a28dae61e51da","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1/AC2; tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","norm_id":"nec59c510ccdc13d0","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer writes a new bespoke extras-parity comparator and a second parallel intended-divergence allowlist, leaving two near-identical drift mechanisms to maintain in one file."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"In the design-question discussion, cite the existing test_no_drift_script_gate_is_verified_only_in_branch_ci / _INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES precedent in tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py as prior art for the deliberate-divergence allowlist, and state whether the new extras-parity invariant will extend/mirror it or justify a different mechanism.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the invariant is NOT \"the install lines must be identical\". It is something more careful: a divergence must be DELIBERATE and VISIBLE rather than accidental.'","Plan: 'the acceptance criteria below do not prescribe the mechanism.'","Prior art in the SAME file the plan cites: tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:1066 test_no_drift_script_gate_is_verified_only_in_branch_ci diffs scripts across two lanes, fails on accidental drift, names the missing items, and permits deliberate asymmetry via _INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES (lines 142-154: 'Add an entry only with a written reason').","The 'deliberate-and-visible exception allowlist' idiom maps 1:1 onto AC1 (fail on accidental drift), AC2 (deliberate divergence stays expressible), AC3 (names which item/direction diverged).","ABSENCE: the plan never references this existing pattern, so a reader/implementer is invited to design an escape-hatch mechanism from scratch that the repo already has a proven, commented instance of."],"finding":"The plan proposes a novel workflow-extras parity invariant and defers the mechanism as an open design question, without considering the directly-analogous prior art that already exists in the same file it cites: test_no_drift_script_gate_is_verified_only_in_branch_ci in tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py implements a two-lane drift check with a written-reason exception allowlist (_INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES), which is exactly the AC1/AC2/AC3 shape.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f243b6657562e286c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Why this is worth its own ticket' / 'Acceptance criteria' (AC1-AC3); the mechanism-agnostic framing ('That is a design question')","norm_id":"n9ffc1c99f3ae2f86","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer builds a bespoke divergence-declaration mechanism (config file, inline comment scheme) instead of mirroring the established set+rationale allowlist, adding maintenance surface and a second convention for the same concept.","Reviewers of the eventual implementation cannot tell whether the chosen mechanism was weighed against the in-repo precedent."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the 'Why this is worth its own ticket' section noting that test_ci_workflow_parity.py already implements the intended 'accidental-fails / declared-passes' pattern for script-gate asymmetry via _INTENTIONAL_SCRIPT_ASYMMETRIES, and that the extras invariant should follow the same written-reason-allowlist idiom (e.g. an _INTENTIONAL_EXTRA_ASYMMETRIES set naming sweep-vs-gate extra deltas) unless a stronger reason to diverge is recorded.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Consider (and, if rejected, state why) a test-layer alternative — assert every test that hard-requires an optional extra is `importorskip`-guarded (leaning on the existing tests/_extra_guard.py + REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 two-sided mechanism) — because it targets the actual drift failure mode with no divergence registry and smaller blast radius than diffing workflow extra sets.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/_extra_guard.py docstring: 'The fix is two-sided ... swaps pytest.importorskip for a strict variant that RAISES instead of skipping'","_build-and-test.yml:812 `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS: \"1\"`","bug 87b8 root cause: 'hard-requires the OPTIONAL grounding-terraform extra ... but carries no importorskip guard'","Plan: 'the acceptance criteria below do not prescribe the mechanism' — but no positive rationale is given for the workflow-parity framing over a test-guard-coverage invariant"],"finding":"The plan does not consider a structurally different alternative that targets the actual failure mode more directly. The real defect (bug 87b8) is a test that HARD-REQUIRES an optional extra without a `pytest.importorskip` guard, so it reds lean lanes. The repo already ships the sanctioned two-sided mechanism for exactly this (tests/_extra_guard.py: `importorskip` on the test makes lean lanes SKIP, and `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1` on the gating lane — set at _build-and-test.yml:812/934 — turns a missing extra into a HARD ERROR there). An alternative invariant — assert that every test hard-requiring an optional extra is `importorskip`-guarded — catches the drift at the test layer with smaller blast radius, no workflow-extra registry, and no need to enumerate/declare deliberate lane divergences. The plan neither weighs this against the workflow-diff framing nor gives a positive rationale for preferring the latter (G6(3)/(4)).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2a4e613649f8b7dc","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The gap' / 'Why this is worth its own ticket'","norm_id":"n96077b8bc0822484","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future extra added to the gating lane with an intended-divergence declaration still leaves an unguarded test red on lean lanes — the workflow-diff invariant passes while the actual failure mode recurs, because the invariant checks install lines, not whether the extra-dependent test is guarded."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Add one sentence of positive rationale for anchoring the invariant at the workflow-install-extra layer (e.g. why that is the visible drift surface) rather than the test-guard layer or the rebar._optional.EXTRAS registry the existing optionality parity tests already use.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the invariant is NOT \"the install lines must be identical\". It is something more careful' — framed negatively","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:1473 test_optionality_loop_covers_every_declared_extra keys on rebar._optional.EXTRAS — an existing extras-registry seam the plan does not mention as the anchor"],"finding":"The plan states only NEGATIVE constraints on the mechanism (invariant is NOT 'install lines must be identical'; divergence must be deliberate and visible) but gives no POSITIVE rationale for framing the invariant around workflow-install-extra parity at all, versus other layers where 'extra drift' could be pinned (the test-guard layer, or the _optionality.yml declared-EXTRAS registry that test_optionality_loop_covers_every_declared_extra already keys on). G6(4) treats the absence of a positive rationale for the chosen framing as a (minor) finding even when the exact mechanism is intentionally left open.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f98303ca7caccc5d5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'That is a design question, which is why the acceptance criteria below do not prescribe the mechanism.'","norm_id":"n434b86a1b32ae1e2","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer must infer why the workflow-install layer is the right place to pin the invariant; a wrong inference (e.g. hard-coding lane names) produces a brittle check."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"df0012b9e33a3847","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["850d3bd91a296922",3168],"description_boxes":["1a0f564ddc603945",0],"file_impact":["7229088fb9585aaa",1],"ticket_id":["cff1b1e62108f056",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":720395,"cache_write_tokens":447542,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4602.2,"input_tokens":1188601,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":168865.1,"output_tokens":20609,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":185881.2,"verify_requests":12},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"bedrock","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock